==Afrikaans==

===Etymology===
From {{inh|af|nl|jokken}}. Possibly influenced or reinforced by {{der|af|en|joke}}, but the meaning “to joke” also existed in early modern Dutch.

===Pronunciation===
* {{IPA|af|/jɔk/}}

===Verb===
{{af-verb|jokkende}}

# {{lb|af|intransitive}} to [[fib]], to tell (often irrelevant or inconsequential) [[lie]]s
#:{{ux|af|Jy moenie '''jok''' vir jou ouers!|You shouldn't '''fib''' to your parents!}}
# {{lb|af|intransitive}} to [[joke]], to tell [[joke]]s
#:{{ux|af|Jy moenie '''jok''' hier, dis 'n serieuse sakedistrik.|You shouldn't '''joke''' around here, this is a serious business district.}}

